  "race": "tiefling",
  "class": "fighter",
  "spellcastingAbility": "cha",
  "background": "knight",
  "backstory": "Born to a house of fading prestige, the tiefling whose name was struck from the scrolls upon their choice to wander was raised in the clatter of practice yards and the heavy silence of ancestral chapels. Despite the obsidian horns and the faint scent of sulfur that marked their infernal heritage, they mastered the arts of the longsword and the shield with a grace that bordered on the divine. They became a knight not merely to serve a crown, but because they believed their inherent greatness demanded a vessel of steel and discipline. To them, the battlefield is a grand stage, and every parry is a calculated flourish designed to prove that while their blood may be touched by the Hells, their martial skill is unmatched by any mortal peer.\n\nIn the mud-streaked villages surrounding their former lands, this knight is whispered of as a savior, a crimson-skinned guardian who treats the lowliest cobbler with the same reverence as a prince. This kindness is genuine, yet it is complicated by a secret, agonizing passion: a deep love for a simple weaver whose station makes marriage a legal and social impossibility. While they champion the common folk with a warm heart, they are simultaneously gripped by a quiet, unshakable arrogance. They move through the world convinced that the stars themselves track their progress, and that their personal struggle between duty and desire is the most significant epic of the current age.\n\nNow, the knight has turned their back on the stifling halls of nobility to seek a path through the wilder corners of the world. They adventure not for gold or land, but to forge a legacy so legendary that the rigid structures of society must eventually bow to their will. They seek the power to rewrite the laws of blood and birth, driven by the unwavering belief that a hero of their caliber deserves both the hand of their commoner love and the reverence of the high-born. Every monster slain and every dungeon cleared is another chapter in the grand narrative they are writing for themselves, a journey to ensure that the name they surrendered will one day be replaced by a title that the gods themselves cannot ignore.",
  "alignment": "chaotic_evil",
